#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# alternating_factorial

#% text
# `alternating_factorial(m)` gives m! - (m - 1)! + (m - 2)! - ... +- 1!.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# At inexact m the value is the continuation `e gamma(m + 2) gamma(-m - 1, 1) - cos(pi m) (1 + e exp_integral_ei(-1))`, which satisfies a(m) + a(m - 1) = m!.

#% item
# Lists are mapped element-wise.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
table(alternating_factorial(k), [k, 10])
#% output
#= [1, 1, 5, 19, 101, 619, 4421, 35899, 326981, 3301819]

#% cell
alternating_factorial(35)
#% output
#= 10046343320261587490171853861825564422981

#% cell
alternating_factorial(1.2)
#% output
#= 1.012247779036864

